    "verdict_key": "undecidable-at-k21",
    "verdict": "UNDECIDABLE at k=21 — but with the adversarial worry PARTLY DISMISSED and the flip DIAGNOSED. (i) The 'Probe A gate is self-referential because the conformal iterate is seeded at the root-test radius' hypothesis is REFUTED: C4a finds the located singularity seed-invariant to ~1e-13 across {0.5,1,1.5,2}xrho_rt — the fixed point is genuine, not the seed. (ii) Method A's real per-parity radii are STABLE across orders/margins/truncation (C3, spread ≤ ~0.10). (iii) The PASS↔FAIL discrepancy is LOCALIZED to the conformal map: C4b shows that with the conformal map removed (raw dlog-Padé at Method A's OWN per-parity s*) the gate fails both parities, raw Padé sitting ~2x below the root-test radius — exactly Probe B's 'branch-cut-biased-low' signature; C4c shows the conformal estimator still passes on Probe B's shared grid, so per-parity-s* is secondary. What the controls CANNOT do at this length is CERTIFY the 40%-split as real ℤ/2 structure: the synthetic controls are convergent while the real ladder is divergent, and on same-length convergent branch points Method A's short-series conformal estimator is biased high (C1a ~30%) and fails to recover planted distinct parity singularities (C2). So neither 'A-artifact' nor 'A-real-structure' is established at k=21: Probe B's 'unresolved' is the raw-Padé low bias, Probe A's 'per-parity pass' is the conformal cure — but the located values are not certifiable to 40% at ~10–11 coeffs. Defer to the ORD-63 / k≈31 extension terms (both methods' machinery is order-agnostic — rerun with argv 63); the specific thing the new terms must settle is whether the odd/even radii stay 40% apart or converge.",
